    {
      "name": "Google sign-in",
      "description": "Issue #11: sign in with Google, linking to or taking over an existing account only when it's genuinely hers. Needs HERHEALTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID set (see docs/runbooks/google-oauth-client.md) — with it unset, every request in this folder gets a 503. `id_token` has to be a real, currently-valid Google ID token: get one from https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground (gear icon → \"Use your own OAuth credentials\" → your Client ID/secret → scopes `openid email profile` → Authorize → Exchange authorization code for tokens → copy `id_token`). Tokens from the Playground expire in about an hour — get a fresh one if requests start failing with 401.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in with Google",
          "request": {
